 do good things at least  he doesn't start out  some examples of this include spike from  Cowboy Bebop who is a former gangster  and current bounty hunter with whatever  happens happens approach to life and  also a great teacher onizuka who at the  beginning of the story is a former gang  member who becomes a high school teacher  so that he can hit on hot girls but  onizuka's character later develops into  a more conventional hero as the story  goes on some would say that a vigilante  like The Dark Knight Returns version of  Batman is an antihero because although  he is fighting evil he is doing it  outside the confines of the law and  sometimes he crosses the line like  torturing a criminal for information  however even a vigilante type antihero  like Batman still has a clear rule about  not killing at least in the modern  version of the comics the reason that I  would classify Stane as a villain rather  than an antihero is that one he is not a  central character and in fact one of the  interesting things about him is how  briefly he appears in the story and yet  still leaves an important impact and to  stain regularly kills or is prepared to  kill people who are not necessarily evil  all in the name of his ideology it would  be one thing if stain was killing only  dangerous criminals who are a threat to  the safety of society but stain is  prepared to kill someone like tensei eda  a pro hero who is generally speaking a  good guy and helps others and cares  about his family stain may think that  tenses motives for being a hero are not  pure enough but it is one thing to have  a different opinion on what it means to  be a hero and quite another to try to  kill those who have a different opinion  than you do even if they are not  themselves bad people stain believes  that what he is doing is right he  believed that he is purging society from  those who became Heroes for the wrong  reasons but his actions still make him a  villain even though his motivations can  be seen as noble stain takes it upon  himself to judge which heroes are worthy  and which heroes should essentially  receive the death penalty even though he  doesn't necessarily know the individuals  he is judging so he can't possibly  understand what is truly  their heart because of this stain could  be classified as an anti villain which  is a term that refers to the type of  villain who has heroic motivations and  is trying to achieve something good in  stains case to cleanse a corrupt society  but the means that he uses to achieve  his goals are evil such as killing or  trying to kill Pro heroes like ten  sayyeda although we can certainly debate  whether someone like Tensei became a  hero for the right reasons to say that  he deserves to die goes far beyond what  a hero of any kind even an antihero  could reasonably conclude and of course  we can't confuse an antihero with a  villain protagonist a person who is a  central character in the story but is  actually a villain rather than a hero  like Tanya from yojo Sankey so having  said all this why is stains such a  memorable and impactful villain not only  is he popular among the MHA fanbase but  he is also extremely popular within the  fictional world of boku no hero and his  actions directly inspire a new  generation of villains including  individuals like dobby Tolga and spinner  shizume a kaguro better known as stain  was greatly inspired by all might in his  early years and he even enrolled in a  private hero academy because he wanted  to become a true hero like all mine  however once at school stain realized  that many of his classmates wanted to  become heroes for the wrong reasons  instead of trying to selflessly help  others stains classmates wanted to  become heroes for their own selfish  interests they wanted money Fame and  power stains soon realized that the hero  society is deeply flawed in a world  where being a pro hero is a highly  respected position a position that comes  with money power and fame 