aying and during his  campaign of violence  Stane murdered 17 pro heroes and  severely injured 23 others it is  important to note however that stain  does not believe all Pro heroes are  corrupt he still believes that all night  is a true hero and he also respects  others who are trying to become Heroes  for the right reasons because of this  not only the stain not harmed deku but  because stain considers that who worthy  of becoming a true hero he even risks  his own life to save that goof from the  winged nomal in that sense we can see  that stain is not all bad he believes  that what he is doing needs to be done  to save society from corruption and  decay many of us can relate  to the points that stain is trying to  get across in our own society there are  many people who became wealthy and  famous by exploiting others by cheating  the system and so on I mean just look at  the banking system and how the same  individuals who ripped off thousands of  people ended up being bailed out by the  government because their companies were  too big to fail stain makes a good point  a point that resonates with many people  both in the world of boku no hero and in  our own world but here is the problem  stain takes it upon himself to judge who  is good and who was bad who is worthy  and who was unworthy and he is willing  to kill those individuals that he deems  unworthy while that might seem appealing  if you are the one doing the judging  imagine what the world would look like  if everyone took justice into their own  hands in the same way that stain does  there is no way that someone you haven't  even met can tell what is in your heart  there is no way for them to judge what  your true motivations are and yet if we  accept stains methods then we might find  ourselves in a society full of  vigilantes who are willing to kill  everyone they deem unworthy how long  before someone accuses you or me of also  being unworthy how long before someone  comes for us because they decided to  judge us before even getting to know us  the reason that laws were established in  the first place was that a society in  which everyone took the law into their  own hands led to other chaos you would  have to constantly look over your  shoulder in case someone decided that  you had done something wrong  and there would be no court of law where  you could argue your point and prove  your innocence so a world full of stains  would not necessarily be a great place  to live in just like a world full of  corrupt Pro Heroes has a lot of  drawbacks and this is the essence of  what makes tane such a great villain he  is not just evil but he is not just good  either he makes some excellent points  and identifies some real problems but  his solutions create their own problems  as well state is not one-dimensional he  is complex nuanced and Hume  we can all relate to some of the things  that he believes we can sympathize with  his ultimate goal even if we don't agree  with all of his methods there are four  major factors that I believe make a  great villain not all of them apply to  every great villain and some great  villains even subvert these categories  but here they are as I see them number  one is motivation does the villain have  a goal that drives him or her and is  this goal something that we can  understand and relate to if we put  ourselves in the villains shoes would we  understand how they feel there are a few  great villains out there who are just  evil for the sake of being evil like for  example Johan Lee Byrd from Monster but  much more often a villain who is evil  for the sake of being evil is  one-dimensional and boring  Stane definitely has a clear and  relatable ideology an ideology that  drives his actions  Stane wants the streets to run red with  the blood of hypocrites and even if you  disagree with his methods you can kind  of see where he's coming from and that  is a powerful factor in whether or not  we end up liking or hating a villain  number two is backstory does the  villains upbringing an earlier life  explain at least to some extent how they  became the person they are today with  stain we see a person who was inspired  to become a true hero like all might but  he was devastated to learn that most  people around him only wanted to become  heroes for selfish reasons this had a  profound psychological impact on stain  and after his attempts to change society  for the better through nonviolent means  failed and he was ignored stain decided  to turn to violence number three his  personality is the villain an  interesting character  do we feel excitement and tension when  he is on stage or is he boring monotone  forgettable and so on when we look at  stain we see the kind of awe and fear  that he brings out in others as soon as  he appears his unrivaled determination  and extreme conviction give off a  palpable aura that is felt by everyone  around him he has a commanding presence  and a piercing glare that is enough to  freeze even an experienced hero like  endeavor  in his tracks stained definitely has the  type of gripping personality and  presence that keeps us as viewers on the  edge of our seats and that is why after  the hero killer arc ends we are left  wanting more and number four is power is  the villain powerful enough to be a  challenge to the heroes without being so  overpowered than once the heroes defeat  him it feels contrived and we are left  thinking that the only reason the  villain lost was the power of friendship  I think that stain strikes the perfect  power balance as far as a villain is  concerned compared to many other quirks  like one for all or he'll flame stains  quirk blood curdle isn't that impressive  in order to activate his quirk stain has  to obtain some of his opponents blood  and then lick it or drink it after he  does this the opponent will be paralyzed  but only for a brief period of time  comparing this to something like  producing massive flames or having  superhuman strength  leaves much to be desired however  through rigorous training stain is able  to become an extremely powerful villain  he has unrivaled speed and impeccable  technique and this is what gives him an  edge over heroes with far stronger  quirks through hard work and commitment  stain is able to maximize the potential  of his quirk and even though he is a  villain we are left with a sense of  respect for his work ethic and  determination and this is why I believe  that stain is a great villain and why I  want to see more of him in the future  after stain was arrested his ideology  was hijacked by shigaraki and the league  of villains in order to recruit  individuals who were inspired by stain  even though she kuraki actually despises  stain and doesn't care about his  ideology at all it would be fascinating  to see how stain would react to the fact  that his ideology is being misused by  the league of villains and how he would  deal with people like him ago toga who  claimed to be inspired by him but who  appeared to have other underlying  motives for the things that they are  doing I would love to see stains somehow  escape prison and then have to deal with  the consequences of his actions and  everything that happened after he was  incarcerated it is likely that this  would force stain to reevaluate how his  ideas are  interpreted and what kind of impact he  is actually having on society which  would lead him to further develop as a  character but let me know what you guys  think do you agree that stain is a great  villain why or why not  and what other villains do you want me  to cover in the future feel free to  follow me on twitter and instagram at  anime uproar and tell me which villains  you think deserve a video of their own  and why if you enjoy this video you want  to see more videos like this be sure to  leave a like to let me know and if  you're new to the channel don't forget  to subscribe and Detroit smash that  notification bell by the way th